NOTICES: the licences of this runtime bundle

This bundle is the runtime of @a11ign/foresay: the program that predicts what
the NVDA screen reader would say, built on NVDA's open-source code. Not
affiliated with NV Access. Its output is a prediction, never evidence.

1. The licence of the bundle
----------------------------

The runtime as a whole is licensed under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 or (at your option) any later version: SPDX GPL-3.0-or-later. The
text of version 3 is the file LICENSE in this bundle. It is a combined work
with NVDA's code, which is available under the GNU General Public License
version 2 or later (nvda-src/copying.txt), so it is taken under version 3.

The npm package that starts this runtime (@a11ign/foresay) is a separate
program under Apache-2.0 and holds none of these files. It talks to the
runtime over a pipe.

2. The source
-------------

The corresponding source of this bundle is:

- this repository, https://github.com/a11ign/announcement-emulator, at the
  commit named in bundle.json, with pins.env (every revision the runtime is
  built from) and middleware/bundle/build.sh (the build), which make the bundle
  from it;
- NVDA at the commit named in bundle.json (the tag in pins.env), unmodified:
  https://github.com/nvaccess/nvda. The files under nvda-src/ are NVDA's own,
  with their copyright notices as NVDA wrote them, and nvda-src/copying.txt
  is NVDA's licence file, which also carries its two special exceptions;
- the Python packages listed in pins.env (PYTHON_PACKAGES), each at the version
  pinned there, from PyPI, and the interpreter below.

3. The components
-----------------

NVDA's Python modules (nvda-src/)
    GPL-2.0-or-later, with NVDA's two special exceptions. The licence text and
    copyright notices are kept: nvda-src/copying.txt and the headers of the files.

This repository's runtime, tables and tests (emu/, q1/, q2/, q3/, middleware/runtime/)
    GPL-3.0-or-later (section 1). LICENSE.

Tables derived from Chromium's Windows accessibility mapping (emu/tables.json)
    BSD-3-Clause. The notice, from the LICENSE file of Chromium at the tag named
    by pins.env CHROME, is reproduced in section 4.

CLDR names (the pinned nvaccess/nvda-cldr locale/en/cldr.dic, put over NVDA's file)
    The names are Unicode CLDR data, under the Unicode License v3. nvaccess/nvda-cldr
    carries no licence file at the pinned revision, so the notice of the Unicode CLDR
    repository is reproduced in section 5.

CPython, from python-build-standalone (python/)
    The Python Software Foundation licence: python/lib/python3.13/LICENSE.txt.
    The interpreter is an unmodified python-build-standalone build, which says its
    builds are governed by varied software use licences (the libraries it is built
    against); it builds against libedit and disables _gdbm to avoid GPL readline and
    GDBM. The licence texts of those libraries are in the python-build-standalone
    release named in pins.env (PBS_RELEASE), https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone,
    and not in this bundle.

The Python packages NVDA imports (python/lib/python3.13/site-packages/)
    Each under its own licence. The licence files each package ships are kept with it,
    in its dist-info directory.

